[9.976399, "o", "Pipeline modules live with the CLI under /app/deskbin and as sibling sources under /app. Spool bytes sit in /app/dropwell. Fixture copies sit at /app/seed/dropwell. Side listing helper is /app/dropwalk.\r\n"]
[9.976981, "o", "\r\n--- FORMAT ---\r\n"]
[9.978002, "o", "CLAT dump (little-endian):\r\n\r\n  magic     4 bytes  \"CLAT\"\r\n  version   u16\r\n  write_stamp u32   dump-write unix seconds\r\n  nstreams  u16\r\n  then n directory entries: stype u32, rva u32, size u32\r\n\r\nStream type 3 (exception): dwLowDateTime u32, dwHighDateTime u32, code u32.\r\nThose two dwords are a Windows FILETIME (100-nanosecond ticks; 10000000 ticks per second).\r\nThe FILETIME epoch is 1601-01-01, 11644473600 seconds before Unix epoch.\r\n\r\nStream type 15 (misc): 16-byte guid, then companion u8 (0 = primary, 1 = extra).\r\n\r\nDigest on the keg is SHA-256 (sha256) of the dump file, written as lowercase hex.\r\n\r\nSequence uses these dump fields even when last-good is not present.\r\n\r\nExtra dumps added under the well, including names such as mid.clat, use this same layout.\r\nFixture copies of the well live at /app/seed/dropwell.\r\n\r\nKeg upload.json shape: {\"batch_count\":N,\"entries\":[{\"seq\":1,\"name\":\"<file>\",\"digest\":\"<hex>\",\"guid\":\"<hex>\"}]} with seq beginning at 1. batch_count is how many groups of three entries the upload splits into (the last group may be shorter). batch.tsv header is seq\tname\tdigest\tguid then matching rows. Success writes /app/kegbay/MARK as ok. Empty well, or /app/bin/clatter pour /app/scratch outside /app/dropwell, exits nonzero. On those failures /app/kegbay/MARK must not exist; a false body is not the failure signal.\r\n"]
[9.978344, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@fd123dfe8404:/app# "]
[10.094683, "i", "printf '\\n--- TREE ---\\n'; find /app -maxdepth 3 -type f -printf '%p\\n' | sort\n"]
